@[grub step]:
GRUB 2 must have been installed into the target in the @[spell-caches] step
(@[enchantment select caches add 'grub2*'], then @[enchantment install caches]).
Its cache supports both BIOS and UEFI machines.

To find out how this machine booted the ISO:
 @[ls /sys/firmware/efi]  # exists: UEFI; "No such file": BIOS

chroot into the system:
 @[enchantment chroot]

BIOS machines: install GRUB to the disk's boot sector (the whole disk, not a
partition; adjust /dev/sda):
 @[grub-install --target=i386-pc /dev/sda]
 (on a GPT disk, this needs a small "BIOS boot" partition without a filesystem)

UEFI machines: the EFI system partition (FAT) must be mounted at /boot/efi in
the target (do that before chrooting, e.g. mount /dev/sda1 /mnt/smgl/boot/efi):
 @[mount -t efivarfs efivarfs /sys/firmware/efi/efivars]  # if not mounted yet
 @[grub-install --target=x86_64-efi --efi-directory=/boot/efi --bootloader-id=smgl]
If the firmware does not pick it up, also install the fallback loader:
 @[grub-install --target=x86_64-efi --efi-directory=/boot/efi --removable]

The kernel finds its root filesystem without an initramfs only by device name
or partition UUID (root=PARTUUID=), not by filesystem UUID (root=UUID=), so
check that /etc/default/grub has these two lines (older grub2 caches have a
misspelled GRUB_DISABLE_UUID=true instead):
 GRUB_DISABLE_LINUX_UUID=true
 GRUB_DISABLE_LINUX_PARTUUID=false
e.g. @[sed -i 's/^GRUB_DISABLE_UUID=true$/GRUB_DISABLE_LINUX_UUID=true\nGRUB_DISABLE_LINUX_PARTUUID=false/' /etc/default/grub]

If you had to add kernel options to boot this ISO (e.g. fbcon=rotate:1 or
video=DSI-1:panel_orientation=right_side_up for a screen mounted sideways),
add them to GRUB_CMDLINE_LINUX_DEFAULT="..." in /etc/default/grub as well.

Then write the GRUB menu (it finds the kernel installed in the kernel step):
 @[grub-mkconfig -o /boot/grub/grub.cfg]
and check that the "linux" lines say root=PARTUUID=... or root=/dev/...:
 @[grep 'linux.*root=' /boot/grub/grub.cfg]

Exit the chroot:
 @[exit]

Type @[next] to go to the next step.
